From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/atomic-helper: no fence deadline on a VRR CRTC

set_fence_deadline() gives each plane fence the start of the next
vblank at the mode's rate. With variable refresh the panel waits in its
front porch until the commit triggers it, so a frame starts about
0.4 ms after its commit and that vblank is always in the past or within
msm's 3 ms boost margin. Any commit whose last blit is still running
then doubles the GPU clock for 50 ms.

On the Nova, NFSU under VRR (ARMSX2, 60 fps, 110 s) took 1755 such
boosts in the intro and 867 in a race; with this none, and the mean GPU
clock fell from 647 to 401 MHz and from 522 to 455, fixed refresh's,
for the same cycles per frame. A late frame on a VRR panel is shown
late, not dropped at a vblank, so leave the clock to devfreq's load.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
@@ -1792,6 +1792,15 @@
 		if (!new_crtc_state->active)
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * With variable refresh the panel waits for the commit, so there
+		 * is no vblank at the mode's rate for a fence to miss. Measured
+		 * against one, every commit is late by the time the panel takes
+		 * it, and a final blit still running then boosts the GPU.
+		 */
+		if (new_crtc_state->vrr_enabled)
+			continue;
+
 		if (drm_crtc_next_vblank_start(crtc, &v))
 			continue;
 
